    "created_at": "2025-01-16T18:56:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-17T01:13:10Z",
    "body": "Apologies for retreading old ground but I feel it's worth echoing again, the spec mechanism for close watcher's enabled state (getEnabledState as a function) feels unnecessarily complex, and I imagine won't match how any of the engines *actually* implement this. An enabled boolean on the close watcher with the necessary logic to update it feels more understandable to me as an implementor.\n\nIt also avoids the need for dialog to have the `enable close watcher for requestClose()` boolean which gets toggled in dialog.requestClose().\n\nNo worries, if editorially the current approach is prefered but I thought it worth raising given this issue.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
